{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('exit-interview.json')\nx={'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-06 04:40:24','source':'Beauty and the Beast (Imagic, Intellivision, 1982), designed by Wendell Brown','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Arcade climbing platformer','perspective':'Fixed side view; x/z gameplay with projected dimensional pixel art','tech':'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub protocol 1 / session client 1.4.0','artDirection':'Original shaded procedural pixel art, layered masonry, toy-like facade, warm windows and a teal evening skyline','animation':'Native Humanoid rigs and continuous pose blending; native creature animation; procedural shutters, boulders and biplane','audio':'Original code-generated chip music, synthesized effects and gibberish character barks. Music defaults to 10%.','online':'1–2 players in AI Hub shared-world sessions, authoritative host including a non-playing server; standalone solo and local co-op','testing':'Native headless semantic tests and full action routes, packaged file browser checks, emulated controllers/touch, Hub harness; no physical hardware or human listening','research':'Original manual and INTV Funhouse illustrated archive; engine API, asset guide, platformer kit, and AI Hub README/shared-world example. Original sound audition: unknown.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux, Ubuntu 26.04 on WSL2','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra','usage':'added on import'},'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],'engineFeedback':['The native platformer controller, dimensional Humanoid rigs, and standard menu/settings support provide a coherent base.','unknown','The authoritative timed-window traversal, authored tower rules and shared-world replication.','Coordinating window collision, reversible traversal, native character poses and shared simulation.','none','Add a documented generic reversible traversal action for Platformer bodies, with snapshot support.'],'promptFeedback':['The source-specific climbing rules and explicit delivery and verification requirements.','The original tower has eleven sections; the plan deliberately compresses it into three authored sections and a rooftop.','Integrating the complete rescue, native animation and shared-world lifecycle in one offline HTML.','Keep the concrete acceptance requirements and move repeated rationale into a shorter reference appendix.'],'aiHub':{'name':'Beauty and the Tall Tale','tagline':'Small hero. Big bully. Very tall building.','description':'Climb the shuttered windows of the Mutton Building, dodge Hank’s boulders and catch Mabel’s hearts for a six-second rampage. Rescue her on the rooftop and catch a biplane home, solo or together.','type':'Game','genre':'Platformer','source':'Beauty and the Beast (1982)','series':'','players':'1–2','controls':'WASD/arrows or stick/d-pad: move and climb; Space/Cross: jump; Escape/Options: menu; touch: left thumb move/climb, right tap jump.','tags':['2d','arcade','co-op','pixel art','retro','comedy']}}\np.write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
