{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('PROGRESS.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\\\n## Integrated verification progress\\\\n\\\\n- Rules: **47/47 pass**. Full solo and couch co-op finish in ~183.44 simulation seconds via normal intentions, default balance, no invulnerability. Solo exercises 16 window climbs, 19 jumps, 20 hearts, a recoverable hit, all six powered hazard clears, bumper reversals/drop/split, 3 pursuits, rescue once, 9-second departure. Full trace/report artifacts retained.\\\\n- Packaged browser suite: **41/41 pass**, Chromium + WebKit + Firefox, real title/howto, keyboard first-window ascent, native pause/settings/dev sliders/reset/single-step/credits, attract thresholds/wake/save isolation, separate pad seats/disconnect/glyphs, phone/tablet/multitouch. Phone composition now fills the width; screenshot inspected.\\\\n- Hub protocol harness: **5/5 pass**, single/two seats, degraded150ms/50ms/5%, host leave, non-playing server.\\\\n- Real simulation network routes: **3/3 pass**, normal + degraded two-client complete rescue and server-host/helper-leave full rescue, normal intentions, equal objectives/ledger/chances/score and tied team finish.\\\\n- Presentation integration: **6/6 pass**, six zoom values, native draw/animation, sim independence, client interpolation, event-idempotent audio, server guard.\\\\n- Actual packaged two-browser rescue and actual packaged audio lifecycle/analyser tests are underway.\\\\n- Important new integration bug caught by actual audio test: title stopped audio and start never resumed it. Fixed startRun/retry resume+activate within the user gesture; no human listening claim.\\\\n- Source gameplay video motion strip inspected; audio reference not auditioned. In-game feedback must be updated from draft before final build.\\\\n- Build README documents run/build/verify/controls/multiplayer. Bundler now embeds full engine MIT notice as well as pristine client banner.\\\\n''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('PROGRESS.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\\\n## Integrated verification progress\\\\n\\\\n- Rules: **47/47 pass**. Full solo and couch co-op finish in ~183.44 simulation seconds via normal intentions, default balance, no invulnerability. Solo exercises 16 window climbs, 19 jumps, 20 hearts, a recoverable hit, all six powered hazard clears, bumper reversals/drop/split, 3 pursuits, rescue once, 9-second departure. Full trace/report artifacts retained.\\\\n- Packaged browser suite: **41/41 pass**, Chromium + WebKit + Firefox, real title/howto, keyboard first-window ascent, native pause/settings/dev sliders/reset/single-step/credits, attract thresholds/wake/save isolation, separate pad seats/disconnect/glyphs, phone/tablet/multitouch. Phone composition now fills the width; screenshot inspected.\\\\n- Hub protocol harness: **5/5 pass**, single/two seats, degraded150ms/50ms/5%, host leave, non-playing server.\\\\n- Real simulation network routes: **3/3 pass**, normal + degraded two-client complete rescue and server-host/helper-leave full rescue, normal intentions, equal objectives/ledger/chances/score and tied team finish.\\\\n- Presentation integration: **6/6 pass**, six zoom values, native draw/animation, sim independence, client interpolation, event-idempotent audio, server guard.\\\\n- Actual packaged two-browser rescue and actual packaged audio lifecycle/analyser tests are underway.\\\\n- Important new integration bug caught by actual audio test: title stopped audio and start never resumed it. Fixed startRun/retry resume+activate within the user gesture; no human listening claim.\\\\n- Source gameplay video motion strip inspected; audio reference not auditioned. In-game feedback must be updated from draft before final build.\\\\n- Build README documents run/build/verify/controls/multiplayer. Bundler now embeds full engine MIT notice as well as pristine client banner.\\\\n''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' tools/check-hub-rescue.py && sed -n '238,272p' src/audio.js && sed -n '128,153p' src/simulation.js && sed -n '60,112p' tests/rules.mjs && sed -n '1,170p' content/AUTHORING.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' tools/check-hub-rescue.py && sed -n '238,272p' src/audio.js && sed -n '128,153p' src/simulation.js && sed -n '60,112p' tests/rules.mjs && sed -n '1,170p' content/AUTHORING.md\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Packaged two-client rescue through real AI Hub bridge/session traffic.\n\nThe browser's clock advances all frame and bridge timers together. Native game\nloops are stopped and driven at the exact native fixed tick without drawing on\nevery step. Every gameplay change still comes from ordinary intentions through\nthe production Network adapter and Simulation. No rule/config/objective mutation\nor invulnerability is used.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport functools\nimport http.server\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport threading\nimport urllib.parse\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nDEV = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nIDENTITY = json.loads((DEV / \"build-identity.json\").read_text())\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, *_args):\n        pass\n\n\nINSTALL_DRIVER = \"\"\"() => {\n  const copies = [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map(f => f.contentWindow).filter(w => w.TallTaleApp);\n  const authority = copies.find(w => w.TallTaleApp.state.network?.info?.isHost);\n  if (!authority || copies.some(w => !w.TallTaleApp.state.network?.info || w.TallTaleApp.game._booting)) return false;\n  for (const w of copies) {\n    const app = w.TallTaleApp, net = app.state.network;\n    app.game.stop();\n    let heldUntil = 0;\n    net.options.getIntent = () => {\n      const sim = authority.TallTaleApp.state.sim;\n      const command = sim.botIntent(net.info.me, { latency: 1 / 12 });\n      if (command.jumpPressed) heldUntil = Math.max(heldUntil, w.performance.now() + 200);\n      if (w.performance.now() < heldUntil) command.jump = true;\n      return command;\n    };\n    w.__rescueDriver = w.setInterval(() => app.game.advance(1 / 120, {draw:false}), 1000 / 120);\n  }\n  return true;\n}\"\"\"\n\nREAD_COPIES = \"\"\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].map(f => {\n  const w = f.contentWindow, a = w.TallTaleApp, n = a?.state.network;\n  if (!a || !n) return null;\n  return {title:w.document.title,host:n.info?.isHost,server:n.server,diag:n.diagnostics(),\n    outcome:a.state.sim.outcome(),ledger:Object.keys(a.state.sim.ledger).sort(),\n    coverage:a.state.sim.coverage,events:a.state.sim.eventSerial,invulnerable:a.state.sim.invulnerable,\n    unranked:a.state.sim.unranked,audio:a.sound.stats(),errors:a.game.errors};\n}).filter(Boolean)\"\"\"\n\n\ndef run_browser_rescue():\n    results = []\n    handler = functools.partial(QuietHandler, directory=str(DEV.parent))\n    server = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), handler)\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\n    try:\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\n            browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n            page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720})\n            errors = []\n            page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda e: errors.append(str(e)))\n            try:\n                page.clock.install()\n                query = urllib.parse.urlencode(\n                    {\n                        \"game\": \"/\" + IDENTITY[\"basename\"] + \".html?test=1\",\n                        \"players\": \"2\",\n                        \"latency\": \"0\",\n                        \"jitter\": \"0\",\n                        \"loss\": \"0\",\n                        \"seed\": \"1982\",\n                        \"limit\": \"720\",\n                    }\n                )\n                page.goto(\n                    f\"http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}/{DEV.name}/vendor/ai-hub/harness.html?{query}\"\n                )\n                installed = False\n                for _ in range(60):\n                    page.clock.run_for(100)\n                    if page.evaluate(INSTALL_DRIVER):\n                        installed = True\n                        break\n                if not installed:\n                    raise AssertionError(\"two packaged copies did not initialize\")\n                page.locator(\"#release\").click()\n                copies = []\n                for _ in range(720):\n                    page.clock.run_for(1000)\n                    copies = page.evaluate(READ_COPIES)\n                    host = next(c for c in copies if c[\"host\"])\n                    if host[\"diag\"][\"finished\"] or host[\"diag\"][\"ended\"]:\n                        page.clock.run_for(1000)\n                        copies = page.evaluate(READ_COPIES)\n                        break\n                if len(copies) != 2:\n                    errors.append(f\"expected two players, got {len(copies)}\")\n                host = next(c for c in copies if c[\"host\"])\n                for c in copies:\n                    if c[\"title\"] != IDENTITY[\"title\"]:\n                        errors.append(\"incorrect packaged game identity\")\n                    if (\n                        not c[\"outcome\"][\"rescued\"]\n                        or c[\"outcome\"][\"phase\"] != \"results\"\n                    ):\n                        errors.append(f\"rescue incomplete: {c['outcome']}\")\n                    if c[\"invulnerable\"] or c[\"unranked\"]:\n                        errors.append(\"route used a cheat or nondefault balance\")\n                    for key in [\"score\", \"chances\", \"section\", \"rescued\"]:\n                        if c[\"outcome\"][key] != host[\"outcome\"][key]:\n                            errors.append(f\"authoritative {key} differs across copies\")\n                    if c[\"ledger\"] != host[\"ledger\"]:\n                        errors.append(\"award ledger differs across copies\")\n                    if c[\"errors\"]:\n                        errors.append(str(c[\"errors\"]))\n                    if not c[\"diag\"][\"ended\"]:\n                        errors.append(\"copy missed Hub end cleanup\")\n                results.append(\n                    {\n                        \"name\": \"packaged two-client normal-intention rescue\",\n                        \"pass\": not errors,\n                        \"errors\": errors,\n                        \"copies\": copies,\n                        \"round\": page.locator(\"#round\").inner_text(),\n                        \"log\": page.locator(\"#log\").inner_text(),\n                    }\n                )\n            except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - preserve the entire diagnostic and clean up\n                results.append(\n                    {\n                        \"name\": \"packaged two-client normal-intention rescue\",\n                        \"pass\": False,\n                        \"errors\": [str(error)],\n                        \"copies\": page.evaluate(READ_COPIES),\n                    }\n                )\n            finally:\n                page.close()\n                browser.close()\n    finally:\n\t\t\tthis.controller =\n\t\t\t\ttypeof AbortController === \"function\" ? new AbortController() : null;\n\t\t\tif (\n\t\t\t\t!this.silent &&\n\t\t\t\t!game.headless &&\n\t\t\t\ttypeof addEventListener === \"function\"\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\t\tfor (const ev of [\"pointerdown\", \"keydown\", \"touchstart\"])\n\t\t\t\t\taddEventListener(ev, () => this.activate(), {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tonce: false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcapture: true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpassive: true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsignal: this.controller?.signal,\n\t\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t}\n\t\tactivate() {\n\t\t\tif (\n\t\t\t\tthis.silent ||\n\t\t\t\tthis.stopped ||\n\t\t\t\troot.AIHub?.server ||\n\t\t\t\t(root.AIHub?.active && root.AIHub.me === null)\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\t\treturn false;\n\t\t\tthis.activated = true;\n\t\t\tif (!this.native.ctx) this.native.bus(\"music\");\n\t\t\tconst c = this.native.ctx;\n\t\t\tif (c && c.state === \"suspended\") c.resume().catch(() => {});\n\t\t\tif (c && !this.analyser) {\n\t\t\t\tthis.analyser = c.createAnalyser();\n\t\t\t\tthis.analyser.fftSize = 1024;\n\t\t\t\tthis.native.bus(\"master\").connect(this.analyser);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn !!c;\n\t\t}\n\t\tupdate(dt, sim) {\n\t\t\tthis.roofBeat = 0;\n\t\t\tthis.ledger = {};\n\t\t\tthis.events = [];\n\t\t\tthis.eventSerial = 0;\n\t\t\tthis.coverage = {\n\t\t\t\twindows: 0,\n\t\t\t\tjumps: 0,\n\t\t\t\thearts: 0,\n\t\t\t\thits: 0,\n\t\t\t\treversals: 0,\n\t\t\t\tdrops: 0,\n\t\t\t\tsplits: 0,\n\t\t\t\tsections: 0,\n\t\t\t\trescue: 0,\n\t\t\t\tseen: {},\n\t\t\t\tdodged: {},\n\t\t\t\tsmashed: {},\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t\tconst ps = options.players || [{ id: 1, seat: 1 }];\n\t\t\tthis.actors = ps.map((p, i) =>\n\t\t\t\tthis.makeActor(\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeof p === \"number\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t? { id: p, seat: i + 1 }\n\t\t\t\t\t\t: { seat: i + 1, ...p },\n\t\t\t\t),\n\t\t\t);\n\tfor (let k = 0; k < limit * 120; k++) {\n\t\tconst intents = {};\n\t\tfor (const a of s.actors) intents[a.id] = s.botIntent(a.id);\n\t\tif (script) script(s, intents, k);\n\t\tif (k % 120 === 0)\n\t\t\ttrace.push({\n\t\t\t\tt: +s.time.toFixed(2),\n\t\t\t\tsection: s.section,\n\t\t\t\tphase: s.phase,\n\t\t\t\tchances: s.chances,\n\t\t\t\tactors: s.actors.map((a) => [a.id, +a.x.toFixed(2), +a.z.toFixed(2)]),\n\t\t\t});\n\t\ts.step(DT, intents);\n\t\tfor (const a of s.actors)\n\t\t\tfor (const n of [a.x, a.z, a.vx, a.vz])\n\t\t\t\tassert(Number.isFinite(n), \"Route produced a non-finite actor\");\n\t\tif ([\"results\", \"failed\"].includes(s.phase)) break;\n\t}\n\treturn { s, trace };\n}\n\nexport async function runRules() {\n\tconst failures = [],\n\t\tdetails = [];\n\tlet count = 0;\n\tconst test = (name, fn) => {\n\t\tcount++;\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tconst detail = fn();\n\t\t\tdetails.push({ name, pass: true, detail: detail || null });\n\t\t} catch (e) {\n\t\t\tfailures.push(`${name}: ${e.message}`);\n\t\t\tdetails.push({ name, pass: false, error: e.stack });\n\t\t}\n\t};\n\ttest(\"authored content has unique IDs, valid fixtures, window timing and a route on every floor\", () =>\n\t\tassert.deepEqual(TT.validateContent(), []));\n\ttest(\"validator rejects a missing upward route\", () => {\n\t\tconst c = structuredClone(TT.CONTENT);\n\t\tc.sections[0].windows = c.sections[0].windows.filter((w) => w.floor !== 2);\n\t\tassert(TT.validateContent(c).some((e) => e.includes(\"no reachable\")));\n\t});\n\ttest(\"validator rejects broken bumper links\", () => {\n\t\tconst c = structuredClone(TT.CONTENT);\n\t\tc.sections[1].bumpers[0].next = \"missing\";\n\t\tassert(TT.validateContent(c).some((e) => e.includes(\"broken bumper\")));\n\t});\n\ttest(\"native platformer jump cannot bypass the 48-unit floor\", () => {\n\t\tconst s = fixture();\n\t\tlet max = 16;\n\t\tfor (let k = 0; k < 100; k++) {\n\t\t\ts.step(DT, { 1: { jump: true, jumpPressed: k === 0 } });\n\t\t\tmax = Math.max(max, s.actors[0].z);\n# Authoring the tower\n\n`tower.js` is the game’s authored content. It declares a 320-unit-wide facade,\n48-unit floor spacing and feet at z=16. All play happens in x/z, with y=0.\nThe renderer, rule simulation, bot and network replicas consume these same IDs\nand coordinates. Change this data, then run `npm run --silent verify` from the\ndevelopment directory; do not edit collision or transport code to move a window.\n\nEach entry in `CONTENT.sections` has an ID, display copy, inset, start X, exit X,\nfloor count, facade palette, windows, bumper fixtures, hazard encounters and\nheart throws. Sections 0–2 each have four climbs; section 3 is the three-beat\nroof. A section’s collision map is built from the floor count and inset using\nthe native `PlatformMap`. The four floors fit the game’s fixed composition.\n\nEach window has a unique ID, zero-based lower floor, X, lower feet Z, upper feet\nZ, order and opening delay in section seconds. Multiple windows on a floor take\nturns; exactly one can be open or warning at a time. `DEFAULTS.windowOpen` is the\nfully usable period, `windowWarning` is the last risky interval, and the opening,\nclosing and inter-window beats are 0.5, 0.45 and 0.8 seconds respectively. A\nnormal ascent lasts `DEFAULTS.climbTime` (0.72 s); it is a native `E.Action` on\nthe native `Platformer` body. Hold/reverse owns the body until one endpoint or\nshutter closure. Never put a window outside its ledge or leave a lower floor\nwithout an upward window. Initial delays leave active floor space for learning\nthe hazard and heart before the next ascent; alternate windows keep recurring\nopportunities available after mistakes.\n\nAn encounter has a stable ID, one of `boulder`, `bumper`, `split`, `rat`, `bird`\nor `bat`, floor, delay after that floor is first reached, incoming side, wind-up,\nspeed and repeat cadence. Every incoming hazard starts in `telegraph`; its\ncollision is inactive until the wind-up finishes. Recurrences keep the same\naward key, so waiting cannot farm a score. Actual instances append a cycle to\ntheir ID. A hazard bounces out of play after damaging a climber, so the same\nphysical collision cannot spend another shared chance on a teammate. A powered\ncollision breaks it and awards 50 once.\n\nBumper fixtures have an ID, X, floor and mode. A `reverse` fixture points through\n`next` to its linked `drop`. Cracked stones use a `split` fixture: the two new\nsmall stones have opposite horizontal velocities and their own swept collision.\nGround creatures scurry along their lane. Birds have a high approach, low\ncentral crossing and high exit, leaving safe facade edge pockets. Bats have a\nseparate dive/glide/recovery rhythm. These paths are state machines, never\narbitrary damaging sine waves.\n\nHeart entries have an ID, floor, target X, delay, repeat and lifetime. They begin\nat Mabel’s animated hand position, drift visibly to chest height, and bob there.\nThey grant the whole team six seconds by default. Repeated throws can restore\nprotection but the base heart awards its 50 points once; delivery of an identical\ninstance ID cannot refresh or award twice. Every upper-floor route has a\nrecoverable throw, including the final roof ledge, so missing the final heart\ndoes not require replaying the tower.\n\nThe rooftop `finale` declares the three climbed heights, rescue X and tolerance,\nheart requirement, and nine-second departure. Reaching Hank while powered\ncommits the rescue and its stable reward before the plane scene. Results and\nthe Hub finish happen after departure. The harder replay reverses the authored\nwindow order, offsets its phase, adds deliberate rat/bat combinations, and\nchanges encounter cadence; character physics and hazard speed stay unchanged.\n\nCheckpoints save section, clean score baseline, awarded IDs, seed, difficulty,\nconfigured spare chances and elapsed time. A retry restores that baseline,\nreturns all climbers to the section’s entry and marks the run continued. A dev\nwarp, cheat or changed balance marks the run unranked. An invalid save returns\nfalse without changing the fresh simulation. No storage is read from the rule\nlayer.\n\n`validateContent()` rejects missing or duplicate IDs, broken fixture links,\nwindows outside ledges, invalid endpoint/timing data, unknown hazards and\nfloors without a reachable upward route. `tests/rules.mjs` adds boundary cases,\nnative physics checks and actual solo/co-op intention-driven playthroughs.\nTheir route reports record which hazards, jumps, window climbs, hearts,\npursuits, collisions and rescue events actually occurred.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
