{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nroot=Path.cwd();old='Beauty-and-the-Tall-Tale-Beauty-and-the-Beast-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-044024';new='Beauty-and-the-Tall-Tale-Beauty-and-the-Beast-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-044024'\ndev=root/old\nissues=[\n('critical','Hub bootstrap namespace mismatch','Network review and bootstrap integration'),\n('critical','Hub replica actor schema mismatch','Network review and replica tests'),\n('visual','Renderer.ppu applied camera zoom twice','Packaged title screenshot and six-zoom projection test'),\n('moderate','Phone framing used the wrong Screen API and was reset on scene entry','Phone composition screenshots'),\n('moderate','Hub HUD selected player ID as a one-based seat','Assigned-seat code review'),\n('moderate','Audio activation could run during Hub handshake/server setup','Server audio guard review and tests'),\n('moderate','Mouse climb request cleared at the first traversal tick','Mouse controls review and real packaged click route'),\n('moderate','Developer bumper spawn used an invalid type and lacked fixture routing','Developer controls review'),\n('major','Native private coyote and dash state was lost on snapshot restore','Snapshot determinism test'),\n('major','One physical hazard could consume additional shared chances after its first hit','Full co-op route and incident test'),\n('moderate','Bot entered a warning shutter too late to complete traversal','Normal-input route event trace'),\n('moderate','Initial authored route could finish without exercising jumps or powered clears','Full-route semantic coverage'),\n('critical','A malformed checkpoint with a null ledger threw instead of rejecting the save','Malformed checkpoint review and regression'),\n('moderate','Closed-window countdown overestimated its next opening by one slot','Window timing inspection and full-route regression'),\n('visual','Heart origin did not match Mabel’s hand','Source/art motion inspection'),\n('visual','Recovery blinking hid the hero during early window motion','Window motion strip'),\n('visual','Ending cast remained on the ledge after plane pickup','Departure rendering review'),\n('critical','Starting or retrying a standalone run did not resume stopped title/results audio','Actual packaged live analyser and lifecycle tests'),\n('moderate','Reduced-motion presentation read the wrong native setting key','Comfort API review and packaged motion tests'),\n('moderate','A fresh run reset balance but left old developer slider values displayed','Actual packaged fresh-run controls test'),\n('major','Primary mouse/touch assistance also steered the second local climber','Actual keyboard-plus-pad mouse co-op test'),\n('moderate','A brief right-side touch tap cut the jump too early to clear normal hazards','Touch input review and CDP apex test'),\n('moderate','Native Shell buttons lacked required hover-to-focus behavior','Menu input review'),\n('moderate','Paused developer single-step did not mark the run unranked','Developer record-policy review'),\n('moderate','Hub settings exposed developer balance rows despite locked rules','Shared-session UI contract review'),\n('moderate','Hub supplied names and seat colors were absent from actor labels','Hub presentation contract review and literal text/color test'),\n('moderate','Long credits began at their bottom buttons and lacked controller text scrolling','Native Shell review and keyboard/right-stick credits test'),\n]\nrecords=[{'id':f'D{i+1:02d}','severity':sev,'issue':issue,'evidence':evidence,'status':'fixed'}for i,(sev,issue,evidence)in enumerate(issues)]\n(dev/'artifacts/defects.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=root/'exit-interview.json';x=json.loads(p.read_text());si=x['sourceInformation'];si['tech']='my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (one Renderer.ppu correction), JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; AI Hub protocol 1 / pristine client 1.4.0'\nsi['testing']='Node semantic scenarios and uncheated full solo/co-op routes; packaged Chromium/WebKit/Firefox, emulated controllers and real CDP multi-contact touch; actual audio analyser/offline synthesis; Hub harness and full normal/degraded/server-host rescue routes. Physical devices, human first-run pacing and subjective listening: unknown.'\nsi['research']='Original Imagic manual, INTV Funhouse illustrated archive and six sampled gameplay-video frames; full engine API/asset guide/platformer kit and AI Hub README/shared-world example. Exact source melody/synthesis and human audio audition: unknown.'\nx['testingFeedback']=[\n'27 distinct defects and contract gaps found by automated tests, motion/layout inspection and code review; all fixed. The defect ledger is artifacts/defects.json. Test-driver mistakes are excluded.',\n'4 critical: Hub bootstrap namespace, Hub replica actor schema, malformed-checkpoint null ledger, and standalone audio remaining stopped on start/retry.',\n'The uncheated full-route tests: they required all window climbs, jumps, every hazard family, powered clears, recovery, all three pursuits, rescue and the complete plane departure. Separate shared-world browser rescue tests verify the same ending and authoritative ledger across copies.',\n'Static screenshots alone were least helpful for timing and collision; they were useful for TV/phone layout. Fixed-tick traces and motion strips provided the needed gameplay evidence.'\n]\nx['engineFeedback']=[\n'The native Platformer controller, shaded Humanoid rigs, pixel material/render helpers and complete settings/menu foundation made a coherent base.',\n'Yes. Renderer.ppu multiplied camera zoom twice; snapshot construction also needed explicit restoration of native private timing state. Actual packaged audio testing exposed a start/resume lifecycle integration mistake.',\n'The authoritative reversible shutter traversal, authored encounter scheduler, shared scoring/checkpoints and co-op snapshot/input transport.',\n'Keeping reversible window actions, native body state, character grip poses, snapshot restoration and remote interpolation consistent.',\n'One line in the full engine: Renderer.ppu now returns view.scale because Game._applyView already includes zoom. Six projection-scale checks cover the correction. The Hub client is unchanged.',\n'Add a documented serializable, reversible traversal action for Platformer bodies, including an example of generic E.Action use and snapshot restoration.'\n]\nx['promptFeedback']=[\n'The clear creative mandate, distinctive window/heart mechanics, native-style direction and explicit complete-rescue acceptance tests.',\n'The source’s eleven-section tower is research context; PLAN.md deliberately requests three authored sections and a rooftop. Human first-run pacing cannot be confirmed by a semantic bot.',\n'Integrating native traversal and animation, input parity, a complete comic ending and authoritative co-op into one offline HTML, then verifying the actual package.',\n'Keep the concrete acceptance tests and delivery schema, but consolidate repeated rationale and add a small reference harness for the required input/lifecycle contracts.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nidentity=json.loads((dev/'build-identity.json').read_text());identity['basename']=new;(dev/'build-identity.json').write_text(json.dumps(identity,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor folder in ['src','content','tools','tests']:\n for q in (dev/folder).rglob('*'):\n  if q.is_file() and q.suffix in ['.js','.mjs','.cjs','.py','.md','.json']:\n   s=q.read_text()\n   if old in s:q.write_text(s.replace(old,new))\ndev.rename(root/new)\np=root/'PROGRESS.md';s=p.read_text().replace(old,new);s+='''\\\\n## Final freeze\\\\n\\\\n- Development folder and shipping basename now include the source year \"'`1982`, following TASK.md’s SOURCE value.'\"\\\\n- All runtime/source files are frozen. Final About/Credits and exit-interview feedback filled from actual evidence; 27 distinct fixed issues recorded in \"'`artifacts/defects.json`, 4 critical. Test-only mistakes excluded.'\"\\\\n- Added final direct-file controls17/17 and actual packaged audio17/17, plus presentation8/8. Controls include genuine CDP multitouch/window climbing, mouse solo/co-op isolation, fresh slider reset, malformed/blocked storage and controller credits scrolling.\\\\n- Final aggregate command will build the renamed delivery and run all validators/rules/device/audio/protocol/full-network-route checks. Expanded real packaged Hub rescue has 3 scenarios, including degraded transport and server/helper departure.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\nprint(new)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
