{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"agent_message","text":"All three packaged Hub rescue tests passed: normal networking, delayed/lossy networking, and a server-hosted round where a helper leaves. The remaining failure was a test assertion that read an old run’s jump total instead of checking cleared input. I’ve corrected it and am rerunning verification, including rooftop and ending screenshots.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');x=json.loads(p.read_text());x['testingFeedback'][3]='The original attract-exit assertion inspected the previous run’s cumulative jump count and gave a false failure. It now checks that held inputs and queued window requests are cleared. Screenshots remain limited to composition and motion inspection.';x['promptFeedback'][1]='The SOURCE field includes the release year, while the filename uses a SOURCE placeholder without a slug convention. The final basename retains 1982. Repeated acceptance requirements also made the plan longer than necessary.';p.write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('../PROGRESS.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\\\n## Final aggregate pass and test correction\\\\n\\\\n- First aggregate: 155/157 checks passed. All actual game, audio, controls, rules and all three packaged Hub full-rescue routes passed. The failed browser assertion incorrectly required the prior run’s cumulative jump count to be zero after attract exit; the duplicate runner-exit failure accounts for the second reported failure. This is a test-driver error, excluded from the 27 game defects.\\\\n- Corrected the attract assertion to inspect cleared held intentions and queued window requests. Added one complete normal-input packaged solo route for rooftop/departure/results composition evidence. Runtime implementation remains unchanged.\\\\n- Re-running \"'`npm run --silent verify` after these covered test changes and final feedback update. Expected semantic route observations remain ~3 minutes for the state-aware bot; human first-run pace remains unknown.'\"\\\\n''')\nPY\nnpm run --silent verify\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
